```plantuml
@startuml
class User {
    +id: String (unique)
    +name: String
    +email: String
    +dateOfBirth: Date
}

class Account {
    +accountNumber: String (unique)
    +type: String (business/personal)
}

class BusinessAccount {
    +companyName: String
}

class PersonalAccount {
    // No specific attributes
    note "Only personal accounts can send or receive friend requests"
}

class Page {
    +name: String
    +visits: Integer
    note right: "Unique name per account"
}

class AdvertisementPage {
    +bounceRate: Double
    +clickThroughRate: Double
    +conversionRate: Double
}

User "1" -- "1" Account : has
Account "1" -- "*" Page : creates
Page "1" -- "1" Account : administered by
BusinessAccount "1" -- "*" AdvertisementPage : creates
PersonalAccount "1" -- "*" Page : "can be granted privileges to other personal pages"

@enduml
```

### Explanation:
- **User** has personal information and is linked to exactly one **Account** (one-to-one).
- **Account** is a base class with a unique account number and type (business/personal). **BusinessAccount** and **PersonalAccount** are subclasses with specific attributes.
- **Page** is managed by exactly one **Account** (one-to-one), and **AdvertisementPage** extends **Page** with additional metrics.
- **PersonalAccount** can be granted privileges on **Page** instances (note indicates this relationship).
- Constraints like unique page names per account and business account-specific features are noted.

