```plantuml
@startuml
abstract class Employee {
    +socialSecurityNumber: String
    +name: String
    +email: String
}

class ResearchAssistant {
    +fieldOfResearch: String
}

class AdministrativeStaff {
    +... (attributes not specified)
}

class Faculty {
    +name: String
    +dean: Employee
}

class Institute {
    +name: String
    +address: String
}

class Project {
    +name: String
    +startDate: Date
    +endDate: Date
}

class Course {
    +courseID: String
    +name: String
    +weeklyDuration: int
}

Employee <|-- ResearchAssistant
Employee <|-- AdministrativeStaff

' Composition relationships
Faculty "1" -- "0..*" Institute : composed by
Institute "1" -- "0..*" ResearchAssistant : has

' Association between ResearchAssistant and Project with hours
ResearchAssistant "1" -- "0..*" Project : involved in
note right of ResearchAssistant-Project: hours

' Association between ResearchAssistant and Course as lecturer
ResearchAssistant "1" -- "0..*" Course : lecturer
@enduml
```

### Explanation:
1. **Employee** is an abstract class with subclasses **ResearchAssistant** and **AdministrativeStaff**.
2. **Faculty** contains **Institute** (composition) and has a **dean** (Employee).
3. **Institute** contains **ResearchAssistant** (aggregation) and has a **name** and **address**.
4. **ResearchAssistant** is linked to **Project** (association with hours) and **Course** (association as "lecturer").
5. **Project** has attributes for **name**, **start date**, **end date**.
6. **Course** has attributes for **courseID**, **name**, and **weekly duration**.
7. Relationships are modeled with appropriate multiplicities and notes for clarity.

